        "comments": "The assembly daHieSnow1.hap1.1 is based on 39x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Kmer spectra and HiC signal indicate that this species is likely allotriploid (3n = 27) with two similar haplotypes (dubbed the A subgenome) and a third more divergent haplotype (dubbed the B subgenome). The primary assembly (HAP1) contains a single copy of the A sub genome and the B subgenome. The alternative assembly (HAP2) contains the second copy of the A subgenome. Homeologous chromosomes share chromosome names suffixed by subgenome (A or B). Chromosome 4 appears to have three copies that are aproximatly equally similar to each other of which two copies were selected for inclusion in the primary assembly.",
